          "S02_PERSONALITY:OPEN_STRENGTH"
        ],
        "blocks": [
          {
            "role": "thesis",
            "text": "The useful question in this section is not which personality label fits you, but how learning, support and absorption enters the way capability is organized and sustained. It is the first reading emphasis, not the whole story: peer relationships and self-position, rules, responsibility and pressure remain present, so capability is treated as a multi-factor structure rather than a single trait.",
            "claimIds": [
              "S02_PERSONALITY:PRIMARY",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:DOMAIN_EXPLANATION",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:SECONDARY"
            ]
          },
          {
            "role": "integration",
            "text": "Capability here means more than being able to learn something. The reading keeps absorption, practice, expression and repeated carrying in view at the same time. A capability may be available while the effort required to keep using and expressing it remains a separate question, so presence and reliability should not be collapsed into one judgment.",
            "claimIds": [
              "S02_PERSONALITY:DOMAIN_EXPLANATION",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:DIMENSIONS",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:OPERATING_CONDITION"
            ]
          },
          {
            "role": "context",
            "text": "The relationship layer keeps this reading context-sensitive. Self-position, environment and expression are connected by both links and tensions, so capability should not be treated as a fixed quantity detached from setting. These relations do not prove a behavior; they require the interpretation to keep environment, self-position and expression visible instead of turning them into a single personality label.",
            "claimIds": [
              "S02_PERSONALITY:DOMAIN_EXPLANATION",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:PAIR_BAZI-CX-PRO-W5-REL-01",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:PAIR_BAZI-CX-PRO-W5-REL-02",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:PAIR_BAZI-CX-PRO-W5-REL-03",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:PAIR_BAZI-CX-PRO-W5-REL-04"
            ]
          },
          {
            "role": "operatingCondition",
            "text": "Reliability remains conditional on how support, outward effort and pressure can be carried together over time. The current carrying picture is mixed, which makes a one-word strong/weak identity especially unhelpful. This keeps “having a capability” distinct from the question of how sustainably that capability can be used.",
            "claimIds": [
              "S02_PERSONALITY:OPERATING_CONDITION",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:TENSION",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:WHOLE_BAZI-CX-PRO-W7-PRI-02",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:WHOLE_BAZI-CX-PRO-W7-PRI-04",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:OPEN_STRENGTH"
            ]
          },
          {
            "role": "wholeChart",
            "text": "Wider chart priorities around rules, responsibility, pressure and carrying conditions also reconnect to this topic. A learning-only interpretation would therefore be incomplete: standards, demand and the effort of sustaining expression must remain visible, without turning any of them into a fixed personality score or guaranteed outcome.",
            "claimIds": [
              "S02_PERSONALITY:WHOLE_BAZI-CX-PRO-W7-PRI-02",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:WHOLE_BAZI-CX-PRO-W7-PRI-04",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:DOMAIN_EXPLANATION",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:TENSION"
            ]
          },
          {
            "role": "openCondition",
            "text": "The final strong-or-weak judgment remains open. This section can therefore explain which conditions belong together without replacing those conditions with a single strength label.",
            "claimIds": [
              "S02_PERSONALITY:OPEN_STRENGTH"
            ]
          },
          {
            "role": "closing",
            "text": "A more useful question than “what personality type am I?” is: under which conditions does what I know remain usable, expressible and sustainable, and when does the same capability require more effort to carry?",
            "claimIds": [
              "S02_PERSONALITY:DOMAIN_EXPLANATION",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:OPERATING_CONDITION",
              "S02_PERSONALITY:DIMENSIONS"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "observationPrompts": [
          {
            "text": "Which of these themes fits a concrete experience, and which does not?",
            "questionId": "S02_PERSONALITY:OBSERVE",
            "claimIds": [
              "S02_PERSONALITY:DIMENSIONS"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Which ability becomes reliable only after repeated practice and support, and which one appears easily but is harder to sustain?",
            "questionId": "S02_PERSONALITY:RB-TOPIC-CAPABILITY-1",
            "claimIds": [
              "S02_PERSONALITY:DIMENSIONS"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "boundary": {
          "text": "This is a conditional symbolic reading; it does not assert observed behavior or predict events.",
          "claimIds": [
            "S02_PERSONALITY:BOUNDARY"
          ]
        }
      },
